 * Run this script using:
 *   $ php relic
 *   $ php relic initiate [--user=<username>] [--yes] [--local]
 *   $ php relic register [--repo=<repo>/<runite>] [--tag=<tag>] [--note=...] [--local]
 *   $ php relic upgrade  [--repo=<repo>] [--tag=<tag>] [--local]
 * initiate, register & upgrade commit relic.json and push it (Specter); --local only saves it.
 * Every question can be answered with its spell instead (e.g. for GitHub Actions).
 *
 * relic.json:
 *   { "main": "<owner>/<repo>", "list": { "<owner>/<repo>": {
 *       "repo", "runite", "note", "tags": { "<version>": { "url", "sha256", "rune", "ref" } } } } }
 *
 * Spells for tests (point them at a fake GitHub):
 *   --api=<url>   the GitHub API   (default https://api.github.com)
 *   --raw=<url>   raw files        (default https://raw.githubusercontent.com)
 * A GITHUB_TOKEN environment variable is sent to the API when it is set.
 */
